<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/020X">Remark <span data-tag="020X">5.5.5.5</span> <span class="named">(Comparison with Pointed Spaces)</span>.</a> Let us regard the $\infty $-category of spaces $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ as a full subcategory of the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$ (Remark <a data-tag="020G" href="/tag/020G">5.5.3.8</a>). The inclusion $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}\hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$ determines a functor of coslice $\infty $-categories $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{\ast } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{\ast }$. This functor restricts to an isomorphism from $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{\ast }$ with the full subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{\ast }$ spanned by those pairs $(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, C)$, where $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is a Kan complex. </p>
